<rml>
<head>
    <title>AdvPlayerList RML</title>

    <!-- Stylesheet order matters (do not reorder) -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../styles.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../rml-utility-classes.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../palette-standard-global.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../components.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../themes/theme-base.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../themes/theme-armada.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../themes/theme-cortex.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="../themes/theme-legion.rcss" type="text/rcss" />

    <link rel="stylesheet" href="gui_advplayerslist_rml.rcss" type="text/rcss" />
</head>
<!-- No `rounded-lg` on the body: frame radius is owned by the style-mode radius
     axis. Styling is utility-class / CCG only; the widget rcss carries layout
     geometry only (anchor, name nowrap, collapse animation, rail pennant). -->
<body id="gui_advplayerslist_rml-widget">
    <!-- THE PANEL is the CONTAINER itself (dark bg + shadow + frame), so the
         background spans the FULL width of the widget. Inside is a simple flex
         row: a fixed-width RAIL + the flex-1 LIST. (Earlier the panel bg sat on
         the flex-1 child only, leaving the rail's ~14dp column with no background
         — the "not full width" bug. Putting the bg on the container fixes it.) -->
    <div id="widget-container" class="px-dp pb-dp widget-shadow" data-model="gui_advplayerslist_rml_model" data-attr-class="my.panel">
        <div class="flex">

            <!-- RAIL — fixed width (w-3-5 = 14dp), transparent (shows the panel
                 bg behind it), relative so the toggle HANDLE can ride a %-line
                 vertically inside it. The handle is the only click target
                 (onToggleAll); its wedge fill is pe-none. -->
            <div data-attr-class="my.rail">
                <div data-attr-class="my.railHandle + (openAll ? ' rail-open' : '')" data-event-click="onToggleAll()">
                    <div class="rail-wedge bg-primary pe-none"></div>
                </div>
                <!-- CHEEKY gradient: transparent→dark overlay across the rail's bottom
                     half, on top of the wedge; pe-none so clicks reach the handle. -->
                <div class="rail-gradient bg-gradient pe-none"></div>
            </div>

            <!-- LIST — flex-1, fills the rest. Carries the canonical panel fill
                 (ccg.panel.general) — NOT the container — so it matches the order
                 menu / top bar while the rail to its left stays transparent and the
                 tab reads as poking out. NOTE: layout classes MUST live INSIDE the
                 data-attr-class expression — data-attr-class OVERWRITES the static
                 `class` attribute, so a separate class="" would be dropped (that's
                 what lost flex-1 and the full-width sizing). -->
            <div id="list-panel" data-attr-class="ccg.panel.general + ' flex-1 block relative bg-darkest border-left border-dark-alpha'">
                <div data-for="row : rows">

                    <!-- Group label = per-section COLLAPSE TOGGLE. Scalar-
                         compared-per-row → toggling re-evaluates classes WITHOUT
                         reassigning the data-for array (reassignment recreates
                         elements + kills the transition). -->
                    <div data-if="row.isLabel" data-attr-class="my.label" data-event-click="onToggle(row.section)">
                        <!-- no chevron; header text uses the theme PRIMARY colour -->
                        <span class="text-xs text-upper text-primary font-bold">{{row.text}}</span>
                    </div>

                    <!-- Player / team / spectator row. Fixed-width slots, always
                         present (placeholder when empty) so rows align. The
                         row-collapsed class (animated via .prow's transition) is
                         appended when this row's section is closed. -->
                    <div data-if="row.isPlayer" data-attr-class="my.row + (spaceHeld ? '' : (row.section == 'allies' ? (openAllies ? '' : ' row-collapsed') : (row.section == 'enemies' ? (openEnemies ? '' : ' row-collapsed') : (row.section == 'specs' ? (openSpecs ? '' : ' row-collapsed') : (openPlayers ? '' : ' row-collapsed')))))">
                        <!-- icon slot (reserved so names start at the same x) -->
                        <div class="w-3 h-3 block">
                            <img class="block w-3 h-3" data-if="row.hasSide" data-attr-src="row.sideIcon" />
                        </div>

                        <!-- Team colour: arbitrary runtime RGB via data-style-color
                             (CONFIRMED in-game). NEVER add overflow-hidden to
                             my.name — it makes the text vanish in this build. -->
                        <span data-attr-class="my.name" data-style-color="row.nameColor">{{row.name}}</span>

                        <!-- eco slot (reserved even when empty): METAL bar then ENERGY bar,
                             SIDE BY SIDE. Each bar shares that resource. The picker OPENS on
                             MOUSEDOWN so it pops the INSTANT you press (before any drag), but the
                             gesture itself is the RmlUi drag: drag aims (we also poll the cursor
                             in widget:Update), and it FINISHES on dragend (a real drag) OR mouseup
                             (a plain click that never crossed the drag threshold). onShareDragStart
                             is guarded so the later dragstart doesn't re-open. -->
                        <div class="w-16 flex justify-end items-center gap-1">
                            <div data-if="row.showEco" class="share-hit flex items-center cursor-pointer"
                                 data-event-mousedown="onShareDragStart(row.team, row.name, 'metal')"
                                 data-event-dragstart="onShareDragStart(row.team, row.name, 'metal')"
                                 data-event-drag="onShareDrag()"
                                 data-event-dragend="onShareDragEnd()"
                                 data-event-mouseup="onShareDragEnd()">
                                <div class="share-bar bg-dark w-full"><div class="share-bar-fill bg-light" data-style-width="row.mPct + '%'"></div></div>
                            </div>
                            <div data-if="row.showEco" class="share-hit flex items-center cursor-pointer"
                                 data-event-mousedown="onShareDragStart(row.team, row.name, 'energy')"
                                 data-event-dragstart="onShareDragStart(row.team, row.name, 'energy')"
                                 data-event-drag="onShareDrag()"
                                 data-event-dragend="onShareDragEnd()"
                                 data-event-mouseup="onShareDragEnd()">
                                <div class="share-bar bg-dark w-full"><div class="share-bar-fill bg-warning" data-style-width="row.ePct + '%'"></div></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>

                        <!-- info slot: ping|cpu (humans) OR AI marker, right-aligned -->
                        <div class="w-8 text-right">
                            <span class="text-xxs text-medium" data-if="row.showPingCpu">{{row.ping}}|{{row.cpu}}</span>
                            <span class="text-xxs font-bold text-warning" data-if="row.isAI">AI</span>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                </div>

                <!-- SHARE POPUP (shared, ONE element — never per-row). A compact box that
                     re-anchors ABOVE the dragged bar each dragstart: it's an absolute child
                     of #list-panel (position:relative) and its left/top come from the model
                     (popupLeft/popupTop, context px; rcss margins centre it on the bar and
                     lift it fully above). pe-none: the gesture runs off RmlUi drag events +
                     a Spring-cursor poll, never RmlUi click input. Shown via `sharing`
                     (data-if). TOP = green readout (live amount); below = granular control
                     (left) + preset chips 25/50/75/100 (right); the inactive control dims. -->
                <div id="share-overlay" data-if="sharing" data-attr-class="my.shareOverlay + ' ' + shareAccent + (sharing ? ' share-in' : '')"
                     data-style-left="popupLeft + 'px'" data-style-top="popupTop + 'px'">
                    <!-- READOUT: the live amount — shareAccentText flips for contrast on the
                         panel (light on the metal texture, dark on the energy yellow). -->
                    <div data-attr-class="'share-readout text-center text-xs font-bold ' + shareAccentText">{{shareAmount}}</div>
                    <div class="share-body flex">
                        <!-- LEFT: granular slider (flex-1). A recessed dark WELL (bg-darkest, darker
                             than the panel) is the housing — it NEVER changes. The resource-coloured
                             fill rises from the bottom within it (its rendered height IS the drag
                             travel, read in Lua, so it tracks the cursor 1:1 — hence the id), and only
                             the FILL ghosts (share-dim) when the preset side is aimed, never the well. -->
                        <div id="share-gran-track" class="share-gran flex-1 relative bg-darkest">
                            <!-- the FILL is the ACTIVE RAIL PART; its border breathes ONLY while the
                                 rail (granular) is the side being aimed (data-if), so the pulse follows
                                 the selected side. The well bg stays constant. -->
                            <div data-attr-class="shareFill + ' share-gran-fill' + (shareZone == 'granular' ? '' : ' share-dim')" data-style-height="sharePct + '%'">
                                <div class="share-pulse border-light" data-if="shareZone == 'granular'"></div>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                        <!-- RIGHT: preset chips (flex-1) top→bottom = 100/75/50/25 (higher = more;
                             position only, no numbers). Same constant dark WELL (bg-darkest housing).
                             Every chip ALWAYS carries the resource fill but sits at a ghosted opacity
                             (share-dim) so the presets are already visible — they don't pop in from
                             nowhere; selecting just brightens them to full, cumulatively from the bottom
                             up to sharePresetIdx (so 75 lights 25+50+75). The well never changes. EACH
                             chip carries its OWN breathing border, shown only while the preset side is
                             aimed (data-if), so the pulse follows the selected side per-chip. -->
                        <div class="share-presets flex-1 flex flex-col bg-darkest">
                            <div data-attr-class="'share-chip flex-1 relative ' + shareFill + ((shareZone == 'preset' && sharePresetIdx >= 4) ? '' : ' share-dim')"><div class="share-pulse border-light" data-if="shareZone == 'preset'"></div></div>
                            <div data-attr-class="'share-chip flex-1 relative ' + shareFill + ((shareZone == 'preset' && sharePresetIdx >= 3) ? '' : ' share-dim')"><div class="share-pulse border-light" data-if="shareZone == 'preset'"></div></div>
                            <div data-attr-class="'share-chip flex-1 relative ' + shareFill + ((shareZone == 'preset' && sharePresetIdx >= 2) ? '' : ' share-dim')"><div class="share-pulse border-light" data-if="shareZone == 'preset'"></div></div>
                            <div data-attr-class="'share-chip flex-1 relative ' + shareFill + ((shareZone == 'preset' && sharePresetIdx >= 1) ? '' : ' share-dim')"><div class="share-pulse border-light" data-if="shareZone == 'preset'"></div></div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
